    "blocks": [
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "body": {
          "en": "A differential equation relates a function to its rate of change; separable equations integrate directly.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "thm",
        "label": {
          "en": "▲ Reference — Separable equations",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "Write \\( \\tfrac{dy}{dx}=f(x)g(y) \\) as \\( \\tfrac{1}{g(y)}\\,dy=f(x)\\,dx \\) and integrate both sides; an initial condition fixes the constant.",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "cards",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Separate",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "variables",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Integrate",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "both sides",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Constant",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "\\( +C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          },
          {
            "label": {
              "en": "Condition",
              "ar": null
            },
            "value": {
              "en": "fixes \\( C \\)",
              "ar": null
            }
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example 11.A",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\( \\dfrac{dy}{dx}=y \\).</p>\\[ y=Ae^{x}. \\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "callout",
        "style": "example",
        "label": {
          "en": "Worked example — Integrating factor",
          "ar": null
        },
        "body": {
          "en": "<p>Solve \\(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}+2y=e^x\\).</p><p>Integrating factor: \\(\\mu=e^{\\int2\\,dx}=e^{2x}\\). Multiply through: \\(\\dfrac{d}{dx}(ye^{2x})=e^{3x}\\).</p>\\[ye^{2x}=\\int e^{3x}\\,dx=\\tfrac{1}{3}e^{3x}+c\\;\\Rightarrow\\;y=\\tfrac{1}{3}e^x+ce^{-2x}.\\]",
          "ar": null
        }
      },
      {
        "kind": "practiceProblem",
        "question": {
          "en": "Solve the separable DE \\(\\dfrac{dy}{dx}=\\dfrac{x+1}{y}\\) given \\(y=2\\) when \\(x=0\\).",
          "ar": null
        },
        "solution": {
          "en": "Separate: \\(y\\,dy=(x+1)\\,dx\\). Integrate: \\(\\tfrac{y^2}{2}=\\tfrac{x^2}{2}+x+c\\). At \\((0,2)\\): \\(2=c\\). So \\(y^2=x^2+2x+4\\).",
          "ar": null
        }
      }
    ]
  },
